{
  "name": "Instagram Folder Auto-Publisher",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "READ ME",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 460,
        "color": 4,
        "content": "## Instagram Folder Auto-Publisher\nCopy .mp4 / .mov / .jpg files into your configured root folder (e.g. **C:\\Instagram-Automation**). Each run:\n1. creates **QUEUE** and **PUBLISHED** if missing\n2. moves finished copies from the root folder into QUEUE\n3. picks ONE file from QUEUE and writes a Gemini caption\n4. publishes it (Instagram requires a public link for both videos and photos, so each file goes to a short-lived temporary public link first)\n5. only after Instagram returns a media id, moves the file to **PUBLISHED**\n\nA failed file stays in QUEUE and goes to the back of the line, so it is retried after the others.\n\n**Before running:** open the **Config** node and fill in every `YOUR_...` placeholder, then create the two credentials named below (see README.md for full setup steps).\n\n**Settings:** everything is in the **Config** node, except the daily time, which is in **Daily Schedule**.\n**Credentials needed:** \"Instagram Access Token (Header Auth)\" and a Gemini API credential — see README.md."
      },
      "id": "4c80750e-b2f9-4c8f-9bbe-320c5efc3058"
    },
